Define SA_RESTART to 0 where the system lacks it (QNX).

QNX 8.0 does not implement SA_RESTART: <signal.h> keeps the flag commented
out ("not supported yet"), so priv.c does not compile. Its SIGCHLD and
forwarding handlers only reap children or pass the signal on; the privsep
channel's must_read()/must_write() already retry on EINTR and libevent's
loop does too, so defining the flag to 0 where it is missing keeps the
behaviour correct.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/src/daemon/priv.c
+++ b/src/daemon/priv.c
@@ -39,6 +39,14 @@
 #include <netinet/if_ether.h>
 #include <ifaddrs.h>
 
+/* QNX 8.0 has no SA_RESTART (<signal.h> keeps it commented out, "not
+ * supported yet"). The handlers below only reap children or forward the
+ * signal; every read/write on the privsep channel already retries on EINTR
+ * (privsep_io.c) and libevent does the same, so 0 is safe there. */
+#ifndef SA_RESTART
+#  define SA_RESTART 0
+#endif
+
 #ifdef HAVE_LINUX_CAPABILITIES
 #  include <sys/capability.h>
 #  include <sys/prctl.h>
